WEBVTT

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.600
The Dorodoro Brothers!

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.860
We overheard what you were talking about.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.110
Asmodeus Alice. Sabnock Sabro.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.840
How about a little competition?

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.000
<i>The students of the Misfit Class 
were given a task.</i>

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:33.640
<i>If they do not all advance to the 
Dalet rank before their second year,</i>

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:39.560
<i>they will be kicked out of the Royal One, 
which they worked so hard to acquire.</i>

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.360
<i>Iruma and his friends must attempt 
the rank-advancement exams.</i>

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.950
<i>First up... The Harvest Festival!</i>

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:24.490
<b>Cunning Demons</b>

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:22.520
"Cunning Demons."

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:27.880
Competition?

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.510
More specifically, a race.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:32.490
Let's see who hunts down the boss-class 
magical beast in the cave first.

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:35.010
If you two win,

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:41.390
<b>D
o
r
o</b>

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:41.390
<b>D
o
r
o</b>

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:38.650
we'll give you all of the points we've earned.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.380
I believe there's at least 
1,200 points in there.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:43.190
And?

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:47.380
If we lose, you want us to hand 
over all of our points?

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:48.680
Nah!

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.430
We don't want anything like that.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:52.920
Right? Right?!

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:53.640
Right.

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:59.640
The reason we came here from the
 battlefield is to take <i>him</i> back.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:02.540
"Him"?

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:05.240
We've been looking for him everywhere!

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.570
Right? Right?!

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:09.560
We finally found him,

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:15.670
and it turned out he was instructing some 
sheltered demon babies at Babyls.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.160
Yeah!

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:23.430
It's a total waste that such a 
powerful demon's stuck at school!

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:26.150
We're gonna become his 
number one disciples!

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:30.430
Once we win, we'll be 
taking our master back!

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.770
Our master...

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.940
...is your master?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.660
What's this?!

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:39.690
Looks like there's an argument 
going on in block one!

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:44.200
The Asmodeus and Sabnock duo have 
encountered the Dorodoro Brothers!

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.200
Huh?

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:47.200
Both pairs are this year's favorites to win!

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.500
Oh, my!

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.950
I can't... see... my students...

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:53.390
Are they going to join up, 
or are they declaring a battle?!

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:56.520
Are we going to see a winner this early?

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:58.880
Wait a moment!

00:03:58.880 --> 00:03:59.470
Huh?

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:02.070
Something is going on in block two.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:20.940
Wh-What the hell?

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.560
I've never seen anything like this!

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:28.520
The magical beasts are willingly 
giving them food offerings!

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.460
Stay in line and present 
your offerings in order.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:34.960
<i>Caim Camui. Bloodline ability: 
Translation (Friendship).</i>

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:37.330
<b>Translation     (Friendship)</b>

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.530
<i>He is able to speak to any species.</i>

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:40.840
This area is already under 
Lady Keroli's dominion.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:43.270
Yup, yup, we know.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:44.670
Have no fear.

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:49.730
As long as you make an offering, 
you will not be harmed.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:53.680
You there.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.270
It's so cold!

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.950
I do not enjoy quarrels.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.240
Violence is the weapon of the weak.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.030
And so...

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:08.130
Do not eat them, my little ones.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.200
A Blizzard Wolf and a Snow-King Fox?!

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.210
They're both magical beasts 
that shouldn't exist in this region.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.290
Which means a first-year 
has them both as familiars?!

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:21.120
Who the heck is that student?!

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:26.190
Queen!

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:26.700
We love you!

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:27.560
You're lovely!

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.650
You're dazzling!

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:30.050
<i>I'm standing out...</i>

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:35.980
<i>I can keep the fact I'm a cute dem-dol 
a secret, and I'm still standing out.</i>

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:39.530
<i>The days I spent training were pure hell.</i>

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:44.510
<i>It was dirty and smelly, and I had 
to summon, summon, summon...</i>

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:48.780
<i>I continued my work as a dem-dol, 
but my soul was screaming.</i>

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:52.100
<i>The magical beasts don't 
understand just how cute I am,</i>

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:54.200
<i>despite how cute I am!</i>

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:58.860
<i>I slowly started to lose my confidence.</i>

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:04.460
<i>But then I faced the weakness of having 
my long-honed cuteness taken from me...</i>

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:08.560
<i>And now, finally, I've found 
the weapon I was given.</i>

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:12.400
<i>I've found out... Yes.</i>

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:19.980
<i>Since I sealed away my cuteness, 
the only... the </i>only<i>...</i>

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.290
<i>thing I have left is my beauty!</i>

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:26.520
She's so beautiful!

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:27.120
Queen!

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.320
Beast Queen!

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.700
My queen!

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.990
I will follow you to the 
ends of the netherworld!

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:36.490
I will be the one who wins this performance!

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:45.410
<i>There are three important skills 
necessary to ensure survival</i>

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:47.760
<i>over the four days of the Harvest Festival.</i>

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.800
<b>Brute Strength</b>

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:49.800
<i>First is brute strength.</i>

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:52.670
<i>Using one's own power to take prey.</i>

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:55.440
<i>There are some exceptions,</i>

00:06:55.440 --> 00:07:00.480
<i>but in block one and block two, 
the most powerful are standing out.</i>

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.480
<i>And the second skill...</i>

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:05.480
<i>The skill one must possess 
other than combat...</i>

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.480
<b>Knowledge</b>

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.090
<i>is knowledge.</i>

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:11.990
<b>First-Year Solas Bobo</b>

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:11.990
<b>Diabotany Battler Member</b>

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:12.990
<i>The ones taking the lead in block three 
are the members of the Diabotany Battler.</i>

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:15.940
<i>Not all of the ingredients move.</i>

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:20.000
<i>Among the ones that don't move, 
there are some rarities that are hard to find.</i>

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:24.560
<i>Those who have knowledge about the 
various plants have a huge advantage</i>

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:26.760
<i>in searching for ingredients
 in the Harvest Festival.</i>

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:29.360
Don't touch the plants 
if you don't need to!

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:31.200
Your hand might rot off!

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:33.150
Okay.

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:35.810
Don't gather anything 
I didn't tell you to gather!

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:38.260
Don't take off your gloves! 
Bring the ingredients over here!

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:43.240
Man, gathering ingredients goes super fast 
with someone from the Diabotany Battler here.

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:44.200
Yup.

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:45.890
And if that wasn't enough...

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.740
It's hardest to see right under your nose.

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:51.270
The King of Wisdom, Allocer Schneider.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:54.340
Your knowledge is equal to mine.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:58.070
And because of that, we've been able to 
collect ingredients at an outstanding rate.

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:01.290
We've got around 1,500 points.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.960
We're going to the reporting tower.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.400
Don't touch anything but 
the things we told you about.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:08.050
Okay.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:09.950
They're devi reliable.

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:11.550
I'm glad we decided to work together.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:16.870
<i>The reporting tower is where</i>

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:21.800
<i>students turn in their ingredients 
and get them changed into points,</i>

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:22.020
<b>Reporting Tower</b>

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:24.320
<i>and there's one in each block.</i>

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:28.820
<i>There, the collector will fill out their 
name and turn in their ingredients.</i>

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.610
<i>The amount of points they've accumulated</i>

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:34.200
<i>will be announced when 
half the time has elapsed.</i>

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:36.200
Welcome!

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:39.490
Now, then...

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:41.870
Why don't we strike a deal, Allocer?

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:47.640
I'm sure you've also realized that 
I said there's about 1,500 points there,

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:51.070
but it's actually closer to 2,000.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:55.750
Meaning, even if we split 
that 1,500 with everyone,

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:57.350
there'll still be an extra 500 left over.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.100
Let's split that between the two of us.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:01.970
No objections here.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.230
<i>And this is the third skill you need 
in the Harvest Festival...</i>

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:06.760
<i>Scheming.</i>

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:07.600
<b>Scheming</b>

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.430
<i>To pull one over others. 
To be eloquent and skilled.</i>

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:15.990
<i>To be a smooth talker. 
To truly be a devilish strategist.</i>

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:20.370
Yup, I've confirmed your contribution.

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:23.310
Reporting complete.

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:26.860
We'll be fine if we split off from the team 
before they announce the results.

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:29.440
Well, I'm gonna head back.

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:31.810
I'm curious about the area over there.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:33.640
Okay. Hurry back, though.

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:36.520
I think you and I make a great team.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:39.130
<i>Yes.</i>

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:43.570
<i>Fooling each other is always heartless.</i>

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:48.270
Hey, I'm back.

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:51.080
Huh? Didn't you go turn in 
our collection so far?

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:53.600
Yeah. I just finished...

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:54.140
Huh?

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:56.860
But the reporting tower is in the east.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.150
Why'd you just come back from the west?

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:00.650
Huh?

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:03.160
<i>And fooling each other means...</i>

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:09.880
The smell of this flower throws 
off one's sense of direction.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:13.760
If he'd only taken a closer look, 
he could've figured out

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:16.500
that the reporting tower, the form,

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:20.840
and the official... were all fake.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:23.510
<i>...the craftier side wins!</i>

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:26.330
That 2,000 points is ours!

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:29.410
N-No way!

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:30.770
This doesn't count!

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:33.400
There's no way that should be allowed!

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:38.620
<i>After this, he went to HQ to 
argue that stealing is wrong...</i>

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:40.660
<i>But nay! It is not wrong 
or against the rules.</i>

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.760
<i>The only thing against the rules is</i>

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:44.910
<i>using an unreasonable 
amount of violence.</i>

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:48.720
<i>Stealing points or ingredients 
is not against the rules.</i>

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.680
It's always the ones who think they have

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:54.670
the upper hand who are the easiest to fool.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:56.950
Talk about naïve.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:58.590
I completely agree.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:01.860
But compared to our days in hell...

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:02.640
<i>Yes!</i>

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.340
<i>We now go back several weeks...</i>

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:15.240
<i>These two were taken 
by special tutor Furfur...</i>

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.340
Yahoo!

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.400
Deeply moved.

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:23.990
<i>...to paradise.</i>

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.750
<i>A club in the netherworld, Valballa.</i>

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:35.750
Valballa

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:35.750
Valballa

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:35.750
<i>A playground for adult demons.</i>

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:40.340
Ah, Sergeant. Are those newbies?

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.760
Just look at my adorable students.

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:44.520
Here you go.

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:47.170
Another serving of 100% demon juice.

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:48.260
Uh, thanks.

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:51.490
And you wanted demonically strong 
fizzy water over ice, right?

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:52.900
Indeed.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:55.920
This little one has an amazing talent!

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:58.780
He can take anything 
without the other noticing.

00:11:58.780 --> 00:11:59.620
Huh?

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:00.560
I see.

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:02.840
That's great! Hey, try that on me.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:04.710
Jazzy, give it a try.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:07.500
Okay...

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:13.870
My wallet!

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:16.000
Wow!

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:19.550
And Allocer is super smart.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.000
I'm super proud of him.

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:25.470
Hey, could you calculate the
 bar tabs for me, then? Just kidding—

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:26.600
Done.

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:27.680
So fast!

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:31.000
Wow, they're all correct. That's amazing!

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.080
Er...

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:34.450
Don't we need to be training?

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.910
What are you talking about?

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:37.880
Creating connections with adults.

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:39.690
There's no better way.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.940
This is also training to be sneaky.

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:44.730
I-I see.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:46.960
Hey, newbie! Over here!

00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:50.140
<i>A place for adults.</i>

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:52.430
<i>Experiencing new conversations 
and forms of leisure.</i>

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:55.560
<i>There is nothing more 
thrilling for students.</i>

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:57.710
<i>They get to play to their hearts' content.</i>

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.930
This is Shangri-La.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:02.570
I need to message everyone.

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:05.220
<i>These two got to enjoy a bit of paradise.</i>

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:08.230
<i>And...</i>

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:13.470
<i>Once they woke up, it was hell.</i>

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:14.230
Sold

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:14.230
Sold

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:18.820
Now, now, boys.

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:20.540
We can't have you try to dine and dash.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:21.250
Dine...

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:22.050
...and dash?!

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:23.810
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:25.610
Wasn't Sergeant paying...

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.990
What? I never said I was 
going to pay for anything.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.510
You'll get some change for 
handing over these boys.

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:33.430
Thanks.

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:35.120
Hey, great to hear.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:36.790
Wha... What are you saying?

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:38.130
Incomprehensible.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:40.950
You see, I worked up a tab at this place.

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:46.000
So instead of paying cash, 
I'm offering you two up for hard labor.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:47.800
They're great talents, aren't they?

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.970
They're intelligent and 
good with their hands.

00:13:51.670 --> 00:13:53.880
<i>It was at that moment that they realized...</i>

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:56.390
<i>Being brought here for "training,"</i>

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:59.270
<i>and being asked to show off so they 
could be sold for a high price...</i>

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:01.270
<i>It was all a trap.</i>

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.150
<b>S
O
L
D</b>

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:07.180
Enjoy being sacrificed, suckers.

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:11.030
<i>This man had been lying all along.</i>

00:14:15.690 --> 00:14:16.770
<i>Question.</i>

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:19.920
<i>What happened to these two 
who were tricked by a bad adult?</i>

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.680
<i>Answer: part-timer hell.</i>

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:26.040
Here we go!

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:28.500
Let us go into battle.

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:31.010
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:33.250
And again! And again! And again!

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:36.760
Good luck with the guests.

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:41.400
What the hell?! 
You gonna come at me or not?!

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:46.280
Humans only exist to be our food...

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:46.280
I'mma die.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:49.900
<i>The amount of time they had to 
spend working was three weeks.</i>

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:53.410
Huh?! Huh?!

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:56.440
<i>One chore after another.</i>

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:58.910
<i>One step forward, and they had 
patrons trying to fight with them.</i>

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:01.280
Take care of the calculations, thanks.

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.680
<i>One step back, and their boss overloaded them.</i>

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:08.550
<i>These two got to experience just 
how unfair the adult world is.</i>

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:11.000
<i>But meanwhile...</i>

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:14.820
<i>They were also seeing just 
how adults worked.</i>

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:17.440
<i>He just hid a card.</i>

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:19.430
<i>How to greet them,</i>

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:21.920
<i>how they drink their beverages...</i>

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:25.440
<i>Everything is a calculated
 negotiation between adults.</i>

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:26.770
<i>Because of that,</i>

00:15:26.770 --> 00:15:30.930
<i>they obtained the ability to figure
 out what others are thinking.</i>

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:33.370
Man...

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:37.650
The game of impish roulette between the 
conman and the fortuneteller was great.

00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:39.100
The tables were turned.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:41.960
I guess you're the most gullible 
when you think you're about to win.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:42.720
Right?

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:44.200
<i>But seriously...</i>

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:46.200
Heya!

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:49.400
<i>Whatever this guy is thinking is...</i>

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.210
<i>Incomprehensible.</i>

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:54.790
You have some nerve showing 
up when we're here...

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:56.640
Okay, let's do the usual!

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:02.640
Which hand?

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:05.150
Right.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:09.280
It's left.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:12.750
It's okay.

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:15.280
I win again! Too bad for you.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.900
<i>A game to guess which hand the coin was in.</i>

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:20.030
<i>If they guessed correctly, 
they'd be freed on the spot.</i>

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:22.090
Yay!

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:24.170
<i>Furfur came to the bar 
daily to play this game.</i>

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:28.800
<i>That dude is totally messing with us!</i>

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:38.410
He's definitely cheating somehow, 
but I can't figure it out.

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:39.720
It's a mystery.

00:16:43.590 --> 00:16:46.990
There's this really garbage guy in my family,

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:51.190
and I'm completely helpless against him.

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:55.690
Because of that, I thought I was 
really good at identifying trash,

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:59.610
but I couldn't sense how 
shady this guy was at all.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.850
Actually, he <i>was</i> shady,

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:06.460
but it's more that he was 
really good at tricking us.

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:10.030
I think that's why I'm so frustrated. 
Because I couldn't tell.

00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:13.080
Actually, that's not the part 
I should be frustrated about.

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:17.170
I get it. He's infuriating.

00:17:19.590 --> 00:17:20.620
Really?

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:22.430
He's insanely infuriating.

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:27.320
That's surprising. You actually get mad?

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:31.810
I'm also surprised. 
I talked about my weaknesses.

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:35.710
You're right. You've never 
mentioned them before.

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:40.200
We've been completely off 
our game because of him.

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:42.830
Infuriating, for real for real.

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:48.880
That's hilarious.

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:53.020
There are many things you can't 
understand with knowledge alone.

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:55.840
That's why I now have a goal.

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.340
Whisper, whisper.

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:02.880
Awesome. That's the same goal as me.

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:05.480
Heya!

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.300
You're late, you two.

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:08.240
My bad.

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:08.980
For real.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:12.600
<i>The world of adults. New and unknown games.</i>

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:16.770
In my line of business, 
masking your expression is expected.

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:17.550
Thanks.

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:20.990
<i>Everything they learned stimulated them...</i>

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:23.200
My makeup skills.

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:29.440
<i>And then, three weeks later...</i>

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:33.840
You boys sure are working hard.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.040
Shut up. Just do the thing already.

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:37.080
You bastard.

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:39.430
Ooh, scary.

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:41.960
Man, you both sure got foul-mouthed.

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:46.470
All right, here we go.

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.890
The rules are the same as usual.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.440
Guess which hand the coin's in...

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:09.240
Hell yeah! It's the right!

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:10.640
Of course!

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:14.760
Furfur never said it had to be in 
<i>his</i> hand, so this is also correct!

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:21.890
<b>Disaster</b>

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:25.880
It took us a while, 
but the two of us figured it out.

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:29.440
Rather than finding out 
how you were tricking us,

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:31.560
we just needed to trick you right back.

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.480
We flipped the idea around.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:37.800
But this is just our first step.

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:40.480
One day, eventually...

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:46.880
We'll pull one over on you 
hard enough to make you wail.

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:48.750
<b>Disaster</b>

00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:58.250
That's amazing! I'm so surprised!

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:02.040
You two worked so hard! I'm so moved!

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:03.100
But...

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.390
Too bad.

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:08.010
The correct answer is the left.

00:20:11.010 --> 00:20:12.440
Wha?!

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:18.060
Trying to trick me is a great idea,

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:22.070
but that's even more reason 
to figure out my trick.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:25.070
The moment you think you
 have the upper hand

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:27.580
is the moment you need to be 
the most careful, remember?

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:31.000
Morons!

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:36.000
But if you just happen to win 
at the next Harvest Festival...

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:40.260
I'll take you up on that challenge.

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:43.470
We're gonna win, damn it!

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:45.100
No objections!

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:48.440
We're going to win, no matter what.

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.310
Don't stop believin'.

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:51.890
My goodness!

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:54.320
The kids in the Misfit 
Class sure are capable.

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:57.270
They're all doing great in 
blocks one, two, and three.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:59.320
It's probably due to all their experiences.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:01.660
All that remains is block four...

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:05.250
And that block has Iruma-kun, of course!

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:05.900
Yis!

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:09.610
Ooh, will he be able to keep up 
with the rest of his classmates?

00:21:09.610 --> 00:21:12.140
So, how are things going in block four?

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:14.710
Oh, what's this?!

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:17.340
The students have surrounded something.

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:19.580
Perhaps there's some giant prey.

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:22.960
Camera demon, could we get a closer look?

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:24.520
Hm?

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:26.800
There seems to be a lone student over there.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:29.060
Ah, so they're hunting a student.

00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:32.850
They're free to steal another student's 
stash as long as they don't hurt them.

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:33.810
Yis!

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:37.390
Now, who's the poor 
student they're targeting?

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:41.030
It's Iruma-kun!

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:43.500
They're targeting Iruma-kun!

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:46.520
Are they trying to crush any 
formidable adversaries first?

00:21:46.520 --> 00:21:51.540
He's in trouble! 
What's Iruma-kun going to do?!

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:27.170
<b>Su</b>

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:27.170
<b>Ki</b>

00:23:25.200 --> 00:23:26.400
Su-ki-ma.

00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:27.170
<b>Ma</b>

00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:29.760
The day's finally here.

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:32.320
Tomorrow, we're going to use 
the plan we thought up

00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:34.280
and battle Sergeant Furfur.

00:23:35.200 --> 00:23:36.290
To be honest,

00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:38.760
if I were alone in this, 
I would've given up a long time ago.

00:23:38.760 --> 00:23:40.830
I couldn't defeat him.

00:23:41.660 --> 00:23:45.860
But your dumb words lit 
something up inside me.

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:48.150
I'm only gonna say this once...

00:23:48.150 --> 00:23:50.650
I'm super happy I got to do this with you.

00:23:50.650 --> 00:23:52.910
Let's win this thing tomorrow, all right?

00:23:52.910 --> 00:23:56.740
...all right... all right... 
all right... all right...

00:23:57.120 --> 00:23:59.260
Wait, were you asleep this whole time?!

00:23:59.260 --> 00:24:02.250
<i>Schneider is the type to 
sleep with his eyes open.</i>

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:27.980
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:24:03.340 --> 00:24:05.210
Hey, everyone! It's Dali-sensei!

00:24:05.210 --> 00:24:07.560
You all enjoying the Harvest Festival?!

00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:08.880
Man, youth sure is great...

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:11.520
Though I'm still plenty young myself!

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:14.130
Now, then... How are things going?

00:24:14.130 --> 00:24:17.600
The kids from the Misfit Class
 sure are working hard.

00:24:17.600 --> 00:24:18.350
Oh?

00:24:18.350 --> 00:24:21.840
I wonder how Kalego-sensei's 
favorite, Iruma-kun, is doing.

00:24:21.840 --> 00:24:23.850
Next time on <i>Welcome to 
Demon School! Iruma-kun</i>,

00:24:23.850 --> 00:24:25.340
"Devilishly Pure."

00:24:25.340 --> 00:24:27.980
Wait, Iruma-kun?! What are you doing?!
